Fins, efficiency, effectiveness and competing losses (@th-fins: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD", #source "../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF", #source "../sources/Heat-Transfer-in-Fins-and-Bars-UFSC.lingua#r_3HAWSMZM80J3ZMZK362ED9E3C1", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "Multidimensional-conduction-spreading-and-shape.lingua#r_59BM6KNFGCMJGXA3QZWGQS39C6") { r_13R9CGJVQMY3Q9XC3EEC2030M0
**Read:** [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), the full fin analysis; [Second Level Course in Heat Transfer — R. P. Vedula](../sources/Second-Level-Heat-Transfer-Vedula.lingua#r_663BY2CF56BBB35C1S595A2VRF), fin dimensions and optimization; [Transferência de calor em barras — UFSC LABOPE](../sources/Heat-Transfer-in-Fins-and-Bars-UFSC.lingua#r_3HAWSMZM80J3ZMZK362ED9E3C1), the complete apparatus description and associated analysis.

Derive a fin equation from axial conduction and distributed surface transfer. The usual one-dimensional model assumes suitable cross-sectional temperature uniformity and specified conductivity, geometry, external coefficient and tip condition. Radiation or variable properties change the equation.

Fin efficiency compares actual transfer with an ideal fin held at base temperature; effectiveness compares the fin's transfer with an appropriate bare-base reference. They answer different questions. More surface area can carry mass, contact and flow penalties, and closer fins can alter convection.

Solve complete constant-section cases and compare with a geometry or coefficient variation. Use [Transferência de calor em barras — UFSC LABOPE](../sources/Heat-Transfer-in-Fins-and-Bars-UFSC.lingua#r_3HAWSMZM80J3ZMZK362ED9E3C1) to plan a measurable temperature-profile comparison, including contact, optical measurement and ambient conditions. Infer a coefficient only after identifying what the experiment can separate from material conductivity and heat loss.

**Continue:** [Multidimensional conduction, spreading and shape](Multidimensional-conduction-spreading-and-shape.lingua#r_59BM6KNFGCMJGXA3QZWGQS39C6).

